WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.634 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Our next guest
is a very funny comedian

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:03.303
you know from her work
on "Saturday Night Live."

00:00:03.303 --> 00:00:06.940 align:start size:94% position:6%
She hosts the 2021
Film Independent Spirit Awards

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:10.143 align:start size:94% position:6%
which airs on IFC and AMC Plus
tomorrow night.

00:00:10.143 --> 00:00:13.113 align:start size:94% position:6%
Please welcome to the show
Melissa Villasenor.

00:00:13.113 --> 00:00:15.181 line:92%
Hello, Melissa. How are you?

00:00:15.181 --> 00:00:17.317 line:92%
-Seth! Good. How are you?

00:00:17.317 --> 00:00:19.486 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm wonderful.
It's nice to see you.

00:00:19.486 --> 00:00:22.288 align:start size:94% position:6%
There's no "SNL" this week
or else I would have

00:00:22.288 --> 00:00:25.558
a chance, I should say, of
bumping into you in the hallway.

00:00:25.558 --> 00:00:26.659 size:88% position:44% line:92%
We do share real estate.

00:00:26.659 --> 00:00:31.398 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you actually creeped
into our hair-and-makeup roo

00:00:31.398 --> 00:00:34.734 align:start size:94% position:6%
when AOC was on the show
to get this photo.

00:00:34.734 --> 00:00:36.703 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is when
she was a guest here.

00:00:36.703 --> 00:00:37.537 size:81% position:41% line:92%
You seem very excited.

00:00:37.537 --> 00:00:39.873 align:start size:94% position:6%
Although, it should be noted
she seems equally excited

00:00:39.873 --> 00:00:41.408 align:start size:94% position:6%
to make the connection.
-Oh, my gosh.

00:00:41.408 --> 00:00:43.977 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, we were both so excite
to meet each other.

00:00:43.977 --> 00:00:48.548 align:start size:94% position:6%
I love playing AOC, and
I freaking love her, you know?

00:00:48.548 --> 00:00:54.120 align:start size:94% position:6%
Um, yeah, that was right befor
everything hit, you know,

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:55.088 size:88% position:44% line:92%
and we had to lock down.

00:00:55.088 --> 00:00:59.225
-Yeah, and you guys did such
an incredible job on the sho

00:00:59.225 --> 00:01:01.694
getting through the initial part
of the lockdown,

00:01:01.694 --> 00:01:04.064 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then, you know,
it's been nice having you

00:01:04.064 --> 00:01:05.765 line:92%
in front of audiences again.

00:01:05.765 --> 00:01:07.867 align:start size:94% position:6%
Are there any impressions
you've done this year

00:01:07.867 --> 00:01:10.904 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you particularly
enjoy doing?

00:01:10.904 --> 00:01:12.705 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-I mean, actually, okay.

00:01:12.705 --> 00:01:17.377 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, Dolly Parton, of course,
and Kevin McAllister.

00:01:17.377 --> 00:01:18.945 size:75% position:38%
-Here's -- Let me --
Let's just shout out

00:01:18.945 --> 00:01:20.814 align:start size:94% position:6%
the second Dolly Parton mentio
of the night.

00:01:20.814 --> 00:01:23.316 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's a big night for Dolly
on our show.

00:01:23.316 --> 00:01:24.584 line:92%
I would not -- This is not one

00:01:24.584 --> 00:01:25.585 align:start size:94% position:6%
that I naturally
would've thought --

00:01:25.585 --> 00:01:27.854
Again, I don't know why --
I mean, you do Owen Wilson

00:01:27.854 --> 00:01:30.290 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't know why it's weir
you do Dolly Parton.

00:01:30.290 --> 00:01:33.293 align:start size:94% position:6%
You -- You have
a wide breadth of skills.

00:01:33.293 --> 00:01:35.462 align:start size:94% position:6%
Did you know
you had a Dolly Parton

00:01:35.462 --> 00:01:38.098 align:start size:94% position:6%
or was that something
that you found,

00:01:38.098 --> 00:01:40.133 line:92%
I don't know, due to request

00:01:40.133 --> 00:01:42.135 line:92%
-Well, it was growing in my soul

00:01:42.135 --> 00:01:44.637 align:start size:94% position:6%
because I found her audio book
"Dream More"

00:01:44.637 --> 00:01:48.842 align:start size:94% position:6%
when I was quarantine --
quarantining alone

00:01:48.842 --> 00:01:50.276 line:92%
and listened to her music a lot.

00:01:50.276 --> 00:01:52.846
And then it was growing.
It took a while to get it.

00:01:52.846 --> 00:01:54.948 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then by that week
in December...

00:01:54.948 --> 00:01:56.649 align:start size:94% position:6%
[As Dolly Parton]
"I was Dolly Parton.

00:01:56.649 --> 00:02:00.120 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was ready
to talk as Dolly."

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:02.021 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Do you just --
Do you feel like --

00:02:02.021 --> 00:02:04.824
When you do an impression
of somebody as positive

00:02:04.824 --> 00:02:08.661 align:start size:94% position:6%
and with as warm of a soul
as Dolly Parton,

00:02:08.661 --> 00:02:10.997 align:start size:94% position:6%
do you feel better
when you do an impression

00:02:10.997 --> 00:02:12.132 align:start size:94% position:6%
of someone like that?
-Always.

00:02:12.132 --> 00:02:14.834 align:start size:94% position:6%
Whenever I'm doing
the impressions of people

00:02:14.834 --> 00:02:17.837 align:start size:94% position:6%
that are so light
and joyful, I --

00:02:17.837 --> 00:02:19.439 line:92%
It cures me. It heals me.

00:02:19.439 --> 00:02:23.776
So, Dolly is one, you know
She's always so positive.

00:02:23.776 --> 00:02:27.914 align:start size:94% position:6%
[As Dolly Parton]
"It takes a lot of money
to look this cheap."

00:02:27.914 --> 00:02:29.983 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's her line.
I can't take credit for that

00:02:29.983 --> 00:02:32.218 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, yeah, that's the same
for Owen, you know?

00:02:32.218 --> 00:02:34.220 align:start size:94% position:6%
He's just like...
[As Owen Wilson] "Yeah.

00:02:34.220 --> 00:02:36.456 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm gonna --
What a beautiful day!

00:02:36.456 --> 00:02:39.259 line:92%
Yeah. I'll go outside. Wow."

00:02:39.259 --> 00:02:42.362
It -- That's what's so cool.
Sometimes I'll do standup shows.

00:02:42.362 --> 00:02:44.998
And I'm not -- You know, we're
not always in the best mood,

00:02:44.998 --> 00:02:50.470 align:start size:94% position:6%
but when I go up there and I d
those impressions and bits

00:02:50.470 --> 00:02:52.038 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I'm changed.

00:02:52.038 --> 00:02:53.173 size:84% position:42% line:92%
I always feel so happy.

00:02:53.173 --> 00:02:54.807 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that one was special
to do Dolly

00:02:54.807 --> 00:02:57.076 align:start size:94% position:6%
because it was Christmastime
and, you know,

00:02:57.076 --> 00:02:59.212 align:start size:94% position:6%
she's becoming
the Queen of Christmas.

00:02:59.212 --> 00:03:03.082 align:start size:94% position:6%
So it was really great
to be myself up on "Update

00:03:03.082 --> 00:03:06.085
and do that impression and sing.
-That's great.

00:03:06.085 --> 00:03:12.258
I can't say it, but when she was
here after her interview,

00:03:12.258 --> 00:03:16.062 align:start size:94% position:6%
she said the dirtiest joke
to our entire audience

00:03:16.062 --> 00:03:20.567 align:start size:94% position:6%
that was so charming and funny
and I will never forget it

00:03:20.567 --> 00:03:24.370 align:start size:94% position:6%
You ment-- And I'm going t
tell you it when this is over.

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:29.609
But you mentioned that comedians
are not always so cheerful

00:03:29.609 --> 00:03:31.511 size:84% position:42% line:92%
You are also an artist,

00:03:31.511 --> 00:03:34.514 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you sort of do sketche
and whatnot,

00:03:34.514 --> 00:03:36.149 line:92%
and this might be a good example

00:03:36.149 --> 00:03:39.285
of how comedians are not
always the most cheerful.

00:03:39.285 --> 00:03:40.653 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
What is that one?

00:03:40.653 --> 00:03:41.588 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:41.588 --> 00:03:45.458 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, I mean, we're hanging
onto hope, you know?

00:03:45.458 --> 00:03:48.328 align:start size:94% position:6%
No, there's a real dark side
to me and --

00:03:48.328 --> 00:03:49.395 line:92%
-Yeah, how about this one?

00:03:49.395 --> 00:03:52.065 size:84% position:42%
Really, I think we're
getting the theme here.

00:03:52.065 --> 00:03:55.835 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, just throw the tras
on this. [ Laughs ]

00:03:55.835 --> 00:04:01.908 align:start size:94% position:6%
-When did you start exercising
your skills as an artist?

00:04:01.908 --> 00:04:02.809 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-I mean, I will say --

00:04:02.809 --> 00:04:05.044 size:84% position:42%
I think it was after
"America's Got Talent."

00:04:05.044 --> 00:04:05.678 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I was on the road.

00:04:05.678 --> 00:04:09.115 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was headlining way too early
you know, in the game,

00:04:09.115 --> 00:04:10.917 line:92%
and I was bombing so much.

00:04:10.917 --> 00:04:15.288 align:start size:94% position:6%
Ugh, you know, to be alone
in hotel rooms and cry.

00:04:15.288 --> 00:04:19.092 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I was starting to draw
and it really helped.

00:04:19.092 --> 00:04:20.727 line:92%
You know, it's so cathartic,

00:04:20.727 --> 00:04:23.496 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it was helping in a
different way than comedy was.

00:04:23.496 --> 00:04:26.266 align:start size:94% position:6%
So it was --
And then I just kept at it

00:04:26.266 --> 00:04:30.336
And now I'll --
What happens is I'll see images.

00:04:30.336 --> 00:04:34.107 size:78% position:39%
Like, those drawings,
they just pop up now,

00:04:34.107 --> 00:04:36.342 align:start size:94% position:6%
like, when I wake up
or something.

00:04:36.342 --> 00:04:36.909 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It's pretty cool.

00:04:36.909 --> 00:04:38.144 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's so interesting
you mention that.

00:04:38.144 --> 00:04:40.580 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, obviously, you're on a sho
that's incredibly popular

00:04:40.580 --> 00:04:43.449 align:start size:94% position:6%
like "America's Got Talent,"
you do very well on it.

00:04:43.449 --> 00:04:45.985 size:88% position:44%
Based on that, you know,
it sounds like you think

00:04:45.985 --> 00:04:48.087 align:start size:94% position:6%
you were headlining
a little too early.

00:04:48.087 --> 00:04:49.656 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you look back on it now
and realize like,

00:04:49.656 --> 00:04:51.491
"Oh, that was a really
tough time to go through,

00:04:51.491 --> 00:04:54.027 align:start size:94% position:6%
but, obviously,
I learned a huge amount

00:04:54.027 --> 00:04:56.029 size:84% position:42%
that I wouldn't have
if I wasn't on the road

00:04:56.029 --> 00:04:59.299 align:start size:94% position:6%
at that point in my career"?
-Oh, completely.

00:04:59.299 --> 00:05:02.568 size:75% position:38% line:92%
It was so necessary.

00:05:02.568 --> 00:05:04.103 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it was a boot camp.
I needed it.

00:05:04.103 --> 00:05:07.640 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it was a cool time
to, like, realize to do --

00:05:07.640 --> 00:05:09.942 align:start size:94% position:6%
I wanted to do impressions
in shows,

00:05:09.942 --> 00:05:11.411 line:92%
but I also wanted to explore

00:05:11.411 --> 00:05:13.513 align:start size:94% position:6%
writing for my own voice
and stuff.

00:05:13.513 --> 00:05:15.515 align:start size:94% position:6%
'Cause that's --
The crowd needs to know

00:05:15.515 --> 00:05:19.052 align:start size:94% position:6%
who we are
and our lives, our stories

00:05:19.052 --> 00:05:23.356 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Can I ask you
for a few other impressions?

00:05:23.356 --> 00:05:24.924 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because my most --
-Oh, yeah!

00:05:24.924 --> 00:05:28.761 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm most fascinated to know
how people react to them.

00:05:28.761 --> 00:05:31.264 align:start size:94% position:6%
Obviously,
AOC was happy to see you.

00:05:31.264 --> 00:05:33.499 align:start size:94% position:6%
I've heard tell
that Natalie Portman

00:05:33.499 --> 00:05:36.169 align:start size:94% position:6%
is a fan of your impression.
-Mm-hmm.

00:05:36.169 --> 00:05:40.073 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, this -- I did it on "AGT
but not on "SNL" yet.

00:05:40.073 --> 00:05:45.011 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I did a table-read "Update
as Natalie Portman,

00:05:45.011 --> 00:05:49.182 align:start size:94% position:6%
and she came up to me afte
and she was like...

00:05:49.182 --> 00:05:50.817 align:start size:94% position:6%
[As Portman]
"Thank you so much.

00:05:50.817 --> 00:05:53.019 align:start size:94% position:6%
No one's ever
impersonated me before.

00:05:53.019 --> 00:05:57.123 align:start size:94% position:6%
I always thought
that I had nothing special

00:05:57.123 --> 00:05:58.224 line:92%
I thought I didn't have --

00:05:58.224 --> 00:06:01.561 align:start size:94% position:6%
I thought I was kind of boring
But thank you."

00:06:01.561 --> 00:06:05.198 align:start size:94% position:6%
So she likes her impression.
That makes me happy.

00:06:05.198 --> 00:06:08.000 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know who else does, too,
is Ana Navarro.

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:08.968 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
She loves it.

00:06:08.968 --> 00:06:11.270 align:start size:94% position:6%
I've played her a few time
on "The View."

00:06:11.270 --> 00:06:12.505 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it's funny --
I can hear her voice

00:06:12.505 --> 00:06:15.308 align:start size:94% position:6%
when she messages me on Twitte
or something. She's like..

00:06:15.308 --> 00:06:17.610 align:start size:94% position:6%
[As Navarro] "You can make fun
of me whenever you want.

00:06:17.610 --> 00:06:19.445 line:92%
I love it. I love laughing

00:06:19.445 --> 00:06:21.781 align:start size:94% position:6%
See, us Latinas,
we can laugh at things,

00:06:21.781 --> 00:06:24.717 align:start size:94% position:6%
unlike Trump,
who can't laugh at anything,

00:06:24.717 --> 00:06:27.086 line:92%
who has no good sense of humor!"

00:06:27.086 --> 00:06:28.488 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:06:28.488 --> 00:06:30.123 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I heard you have
a Kristen Wiig, as well.

00:06:30.123 --> 00:06:32.191 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't think I've ever hear
a Kristen Wiig.

00:06:32.191 --> 00:06:35.228 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[As Wiig]
"Oh. I -- I do Kristen Wiig.

00:06:35.228 --> 00:06:36.796 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Whoa! Whoa!

00:06:36.796 --> 00:06:38.698 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-[ Laughs ]

00:06:38.698 --> 00:06:43.836 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I love to play Kristen,
and I'm --

00:06:43.836 --> 00:06:45.104 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I'm just the best."

00:06:45.104 --> 00:06:48.040 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't know. Yeah.
That's my Kristen.

00:06:48.040 --> 00:06:51.477 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think I auditioned
with a silly bit

00:06:51.477 --> 00:06:55.348
of Kristen Wiig
about to go skydiving, you know,

00:06:55.348 --> 00:06:57.283 align:start size:94% position:6%
and she's just
in the plane like...

00:06:57.283 --> 00:06:58.451 align:start size:94% position:6%
[As Wiig]
"I...change my mind.

00:06:58.451 --> 00:07:03.723 align:start size:94% position:6%
I -- I'm -- I'm scared.
I -- I don't want to go. I'm -

00:07:03.723 --> 00:07:05.925 align:start size:94% position:6%
'Cause then I'll get stuck
on a cloud

00:07:05.925 --> 00:07:07.493 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I'll have to
become an angel."

00:07:07.493 --> 00:07:10.096 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-Wow. That one is --

00:07:10.096 --> 00:07:11.831 line:92%
I, like, want to call Kriste

00:07:11.831 --> 00:07:15.768 align:start size:94% position:6%
and make sure
she still has her soul.

00:07:15.768 --> 00:07:20.173 size:81% position:41%
Hey, it is just great
to see you, as always.

00:07:20.173 --> 00:07:23.676 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thank you so much for
making time for us, Melissa.

00:07:23.676 --> 00:07:24.243 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Very exciting.

00:07:24.243 --> 00:07:26.879 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, I know you've already
filmed your monologue

00:07:26.879 --> 00:07:27.947 align:start size:94% position:6%
for the Independent
Spirit Awards.

00:07:27.947 --> 00:07:30.983
You must be excited to see i
all come together, though.

00:07:30.983 --> 00:07:34.620 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm so excited.
I'm very proud of doing that

00:07:34.620 --> 00:07:39.292 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's an honor,
and I felt like --

00:07:39.292 --> 00:07:40.259 line:92%
I want to do more hosting,

00:07:40.259 --> 00:07:42.929
and I would love to with
a crowd, because it's fun.

00:07:42.929 --> 00:07:45.164 align:start size:94% position:6%
You get to share everything.
You get to --

00:07:45.164 --> 00:07:48.868
I did impressions and singin
and myself as a monologue.

00:07:48.868 --> 00:07:51.204 size:84% position:42%
And it's just like --
Ugh, I want to do more.

00:07:51.204 --> 00:07:53.739 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was so fun,
and I hope people enjoy.

00:07:53.739 --> 00:07:54.707 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-I can't wait to see it.

00:07:54.707 --> 00:07:57.276 align:start size:94% position:6%
I can't wait to watch
the end of this "SNL" season

00:07:57.276 --> 00:08:00.379 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I look forward
to seeing you soon in person

00:08:00.379 --> 00:08:01.647 line:92%
-Yep. Good to see you, Seth.

00:08:01.647 --> 00:08:03.549 align:start size:94% position:6%
-The Film Independent
Spirit Awards

00:08:03.549 --> 00:08:05.585 align:start size:94% position:6%
air tomorrow night
on IFC and AMC Plus.

00:08:05.585 --> 00:08:09.021 align:start size:94% position:6%
We'll be right back
with more "Late Night."

